 "A month with nothing done is the point to involve your council. This is free, it does not need a solicitor, and it is the route landlords take most seriously.": "",
 "Councils assess housing hazards partly on who is exposed to them. A household including a child, an older person or someone with asthma or another respiratory condition raises the severity score, and that changes what the council can require your landlord to do. Never leave it out.": "",
 "If the extractor fan in your bathroom or kitchen does not work, say so explicitly in writing. It is a concrete defect, it is cheap to fix, and it undercuts the lifestyle argument immediately.": "",
 "Soft, dark, crumbling wood in a wet area. Contained and fixable — but the water reaching it has not been stopped, so replacing the timber alone buys about a year.": "",
 "Two months. If private, report the landlord to Rent Smart Wales. If social, your complaint should be through their process and ready for the Public Services Ombudsman for Wales.": "",
 "Water crossing the wall from outside through a specific fault: cracked render, failed pointing, a split downpipe, a slipped slate, a chimney flashing. It is a building repair and squarely a landlord repair. Say in your letter that it worsens after rain — that detail does a lot of work.": ""
}